Atari TOS 1.62
--------------

This project ships no Atari ROM, no part of one, and no image derived from one.

An Atari TOS 1.62 image is proprietary software owned by Atari Interactive, Inc. / Atari SA. It can
only be supplied by the user, from a machine or medium they own. The project holds no licence to
distribute it and does not: the emulator validates a user-supplied image against a pinned SHA-256
accept-list (`roms/tos-hashes.json`) and refuses anything else.

See docs/adr/0010-tos-image-provisioning.md.


The 680x0 single-step corpus
----------------------------

`tests/680x0/` carries a sample of Thomas Harte's 68000 single-step test set, vendored as test data
from `SingleStepTests/680x0` at commit `e0d5ece` (2024-05-13). Upstream declares no licence; the corpus
is used here for local verification only and is not built into, shipped with or licensed as part of
The ST. The full corpus is fetched on demand by `scripts/fetch-680x0-tests.sh` and never committed.

    Author:  Thomas Harte <thomas.harte@gmail.com>
    Source:  https://github.com/SingleStepTests/680x0

The hardware-based conformance set
----------------------------------

`tests/680x0/conformance/` carries two sources that are tied to real silicon, with the ledger of what
each checks in `tests/680x0/CONFORMANCE.md`:

`flamewing-bcd/bcd-table.bin` — the exhaustive ABCD/SBCD/NBCD expectation table (525 312 entries)
generated by flamewing's BCD verifier, whose test ROM passes on a Model 1 and a Model 3 VA2 Sega
Genesis. Generated data, vendored as test data for local verification only; regenerated from the pin by
`scripts/fetch-conformance.sh`.

    Author:  Marzo Sette Torres Junior (flamewing)
    Source:  https://github.com/flamewing/68k-bcd-verifier at 39a01be
    Licence: GNU General Public License, version 3 — the generator, not the table

`winuae-cputest/` — `readme.txt` and `cputestgen.ini`, the recipe and preset list of WinUAE's CPU
tester, the 68000 core Toni Wilen corrects against real Amigas. Configuration and documentation files
only; the expected values are generated by that tester core and are not vendored.

    Author:  Toni Wilen
    Source:  https://github.com/tonioni/WinUAE at 1977af5 (cputest/)
    Licence: GNU General Public License, version 2 or later — see WinUAE's own licence



